index 0000000..18834ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/rojo-workflow.md
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+# Working with Rojo day to day
+
+Git is the source of truth for this game. Code lives in files under `src/`, and `rojo serve`
+syncs those files into **your own dev place** in Studio. Studio is where you run, test, and
+playtest. You don't edit code there.
+
+## First-time setup
+
+1. Install the tools with `rokit install`. Packages come from `pesde install` here and again in
+   `test_packages/`.
+2. Make your own dev place in Studio, a copy of the Baseplate place. Never serve into a shared or
+   live place.
+3. Add your dev place's id to `servePlaceIds` in `default.project.json`. Rojo then refuses to sync
+   into any other place, so a stray Connect can't overwrite someone else's work.
+4. Run `rojo serve` from the repo root (port 34872), open your dev place, and click **Connect** in
+   the Rojo plugin.
+
+## Where to make changes
+
+- **Make every change in the files under `src/`.** README.md's Layout table shows where each
+  folder lands in the place. A script you edit in Studio is overwritten by the next sync, and
+  Git never sees the edit. The same goes for a property, attribute, tag, or new instance under a
+  synced folder.
+- File names decide instance types: `*.server.luau` is a Script, `*.client.luau` is a LocalScript,
+  and any other `.luau` file is a ModuleScript. Jest specs go in
+  `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs` as `Name.spec.luau`.
+- Attributes and tags go in a `Name.meta.json` beside the file (or `init.meta.json` in a folder).
+- **Never edit `roblox_packages/` or `test_packages/roblox_packages/`.** pesde regenerates them,
+  and the files are hardlinked to a store other projects share. Change `pesde.toml` and
+  reinstall instead. Require packages through their links (`ReplicatedStorage.Packages.Vide`),
+  never through a `.pesde/...` path.
+- If you really do build something in Studio (a model, a GUI), save it back over its `.rbxm` file
+  with **Save to File**, or ask about `rojo syncback`. Otherwise the next sync deletes it.
+- Work on your own branch. When working in parallel, use your own `git worktree` with its own
+  `rojo serve --port`.
+
+## What to check while serving
+
+- **Is your change actually in Studio?** After saving, open the script in Studio and check that
+  the new text is there before you playtest or run specs. A check that runs too early tests the
+  old code.
+- **Is `rojo serve` still running?** Rojo 7.7.0 and 7.7.1 sometimes crash (`Rojo crashed!` ...
+  `change_processor.rs`) when you delete, move, or rename a file or folder. Studio then quietly
+  stops getting changes. After a delete or rename, look at the serve terminal. If it died,
+  restart `rojo serve` and click Connect again.
+- **Which code is being served?** Rojo serves the folder it was started in, on whatever branch is
+  checked out there. A merged pull request changes nothing locally until you pull.
+- **Stop `rojo serve` first** before anything that rewrites many files at once: `git checkout`,
+  `switch`, `pull`, `rebase`, `reset`, `stash`, `pesde install`, or a bulk delete. Restart it
+  afterward.
+- Before pushing, run the checks from README.md (`rojo sourcemap`, `luau-lsp analyze`, `selene`,
+  `stylua --check`) and run the specs in Studio.
+
+## Don't break `default.project.json`
+
+`default.project.json` decides where every folder lands in the place. A bad edit can break
+Studio sync, luau-lsp, and Jest all at once. In past breakages, `StarterPlayerScripts` lost its
+final `s`, the Jest packages ended up in `ReplicatedStorage` instead of
+`ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`, and the file was saved with a byte order mark.
+
+- **Edit it only when the layout is really changing**, and update README.md's Layout table in
+  the same commit. The table and the project file must agree.
+- **Keep `globIgnorePaths` and the `Tests` node together.** `ServerScriptService` mounts all of
+  `src/ServerScriptService`. `Tests` is mounted again as its own node so that the Jest packages
+  can sit beside `Specs`, and `globIgnorePaths` stops the first mount from adding a second
+  `Tests` folder.
+- **Save it as UTF-8 without a BOM.** Rojo fails with `Failed to parse JSONC` on a file that
+  starts with one. Windows PowerShell 5.1's `Set-Content`/`Out-File` and some editors add it. To
+  check, run `head -c 3 default.project.json | od -An -tx1` in Git Bash; the output must not be
+  `ef bb bf`.
+- **Resolving a merge conflict in it:** don't just pick one side. Keep both sides' intent, then
+  compare the result against the Layout table, path by path. Look out for typos in `$path`
+  values, since a path that doesn't exist fails the whole project.
+- **Validate before committing** with:
+
+  ```sh
+  rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts
+  ```
+
+  It must succeed. Spot-check `sourcemap.json`: you should see one `Tests` folder holding `Specs`
+  and `Packages` (with `Jest` and `JestGlobals`), and `StarterPlayerScripts` holding
+  `Main.client.luau`.
+- Ask for a review on any pull request that touches the project file.
